<article class="env-lemma" id="02UR">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02UR">Lemma <span data-tag="02UR">10.151.6</span>.</a> Let $R \to S$ be a finite type ring map. Let $\mathfrak q$ be a prime of $S$. If $R \to S$ is unramified at $\mathfrak q$ then $R \to S$ is quasi-finite at $\mathfrak q$. In particular, an unramified ring map is quasi-finite. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      An unramified ring map is of finite type. Thus it is clear that the second statement follows from the first. To see the first statement apply the characterization of Lemma <a href="/tag/00PK" data-tag="00PK">10.122.2</a> part (2) using Lemma <a href="/tag/00UW" data-tag="00UW">10.151.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>